& [SJS]
  + Situation: exact checkpoints are replay-complete but unnecessarily large as scheduling or model-facing handles
  + Justification: a minimal handle can carry phase operation and commitments while exact checkpoint bytes stay under host custody
  + Solution: compile a strict bound handle and measure it against every full checkpoint before considering it an optimization

& [Delineation]
  + handle local validity means closed shape and digest syntax only
  + handle-to-checkpoint binding requires host recomputation
  + checkpoint custody availability is asserted only as fixture structure and not physical persistence proof
  + byte savings are transport evidence and not tokenizer or model-quality evidence

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + handle carries only operation identity positioning two or three content commitments and claim limits
  + response digest presence is derived from checkpoint phase
  + measurement retains each exact handle and both byte counts so all aggregates rederive
  + signed arithmetic and basis-point ratio use checked conversions

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty separates locator integrity host binding persistence and performance claims
  + Security binds the complete checkpoint under a handle-specific digest domain
  + Planner preserves phase next-operation position and terminal identity
  + Weaver joins minimal handle to exact checkpoint custody
  + Scribe records case-level and aggregate byte evidence
  + Refiner removes full trace request and response bodies from the compact surface
  + Observer rederives all mappings and measurement arithmetic

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated checkpoint_handle forms validators measurement CLI output artifact and adversarial tests
  + keep live provider tokenizer and persistence experiments outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module CLI branch artifact exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior
